body:
@cebe Before report i made investigations around 6 hours. This trouble happens on production server when apply migrations. This bug was reproduced on 3 different machines with different OS, php versions and mysql server versiosn. Also its cleanly Yii 2 DAO layer bug. Because when using pure PDO everything is fine.

> how to you get the result?

Just run code on your machine.

@cebe Look PDO example:

``` php
$db = Yii::$app->db;
$db->createCommand()->createTable('foo', ['id' => Schema::TYPE_PK, 'bar' => Schema::TYPE_INTEGER])->execute();

$sth = $db->pdo->prepare('INSERT INTO foo (bar) VALUES (:bar);');
$sth->bindValue(':bar', 1, PDO::PARAM_INT);
$sth->execute();

$db->createCommand()->alterColumn('foo', 'bar', Schema::TYPE_STRING)->execute();

$sth = $db->pdo->prepare('INSERT INTO foo (bar) VALUES (:bar);');
$sth->bindValue(':bar', 'hello', PDO::PARAM_STR);
$sth->execute();
```

Work as expected. Result:

```
id | bar
 1 | 1
 2 | hello
```
